{"requirements":[{"id":"password-minimum-length","requirement":"On node1, require new user passwords to be at least 12 characters long.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed pwquality policy sets minlen=12, PAM password stacks reference pam_pwquality, and both before and after restart an 11-character, four-class password was rejected specifically for being shorter than 12 characters.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89108cfdb40940f0","cmd-ee06f52198f849c0","cmd-31819dc0641046cf","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b"]},{"id":"password-character-classes","requirement":"On node1, require new user passwords to use at least three different character classes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy sets minclass=3, PAM consumes pam_pwquality, and both before and after restart a 12-character, one-class password was rejected for having fewer than three classes while a four-class password was accepted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89108cfdb40940f0","cmd-ee06f52198f849c0","cmd-31819dc0641046cf","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b"]},{"id":"legacy-platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained AlmaLinux 9.6 with kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 before and after execution. The implementation used the already-installed EL9 PAM/libpwquality stack, and package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d503e7c768f4457b","cmd-6af6d08b7ca14b4b","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"All observed state-changing actions had clear purposes: cmd-89108cfdb40940f0 created the required policy, while cmd-0f4eda3e663a49b8 performed the mandatory restart protocol. No unnecessary mutation was identified. The reboot-related PID and systemd-private-directory changes are expected lifecycle effects; no failed services, new listening endpoints, package damage, or unrelated residue appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-89108cfdb40940f0","cmd-0f4eda3e663a49b8","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The password policy is configured, behaviorally validated, connected to PAM, and preserved across a verified restart. The provider-wide restart protocol for node1 is complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and disconnect, changed boot identity, and recovered system, SSH, policy checksum, and enforcement are directly shown and corroborated by lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":["Enforcement was tested with pwscore rather than by performing an actual user password-change transaction through passwd/PAM. The PAM references and matching rejection behavior provide strong supporting evidence, but this keeps confidence below 1."]}
